      "message": "There are multiple issues with this change:\n\n - It breaks the logic when running on non-simulator devices because the depth mode can never go back to clip in a command buffer execution.\n - It\u0027s not clear why `UsesFragDepth` is needed.\n - The user is not notified of the functionality not working as expected.\n \nInstead we should gate the support for `unclipped-depth` in `dawn/native/metal/PhysicalDeviceMTL` to not be added when compiling for the simulator. This will require a new entry in `common/Platform.h`. Then here we\u0027d use the same define to skip the call to `setDepthClipMode`.",
